A||||1||wardog85GT||rear wiring harness Q's||||1||
Z||000000||wardog85GT||12-02-2001||11:33 AM||||I own an 85 GT and recently one of the wires grounded out and burned apart while I was driving. Now I have no power to the cars electrical system when the key is turned on. The wire ran into the rear junction block on the passenger side firewall. Can I replace it with a 4 cyl. harness?||||reg||1
Z||000001||skitime||12-02-2001||12:57 PM||||There is a good chance what burned out was what is called a fuseable link.  It is designed to "burn out" like a fuse.  If is the fuseable link you can buy another at a auto parts supply store.  These wires are designed to burn up to protect the rest of the wiring harness and are orange at that juction box. There is a chance the wire was fatigued but is an indication of a "heavy short" somewhere.  Often a bad connection around the starter can create this.  I would not be too quick to replace the entire wiring harness.  Determine which wire burned and where it goes and look along the harness from the junction box to the other end.  Good Luck!<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
